<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Merged into the bundle's Info.plist by the Tauri CLI on macOS.

  Without NSMicrophoneUsageDescription macOS does not even ask: the capture
  callback simply delivers zeros, and a silent channel is indistinguishable
  from a denied permission. That is the failure the plan flags as the main
  risk in P1, so the key is here from the start rather than at packaging time.

  P13 additionally needs the `com.apple.security.device.audio-input`
  entitlement, because Hardened Runtime gates the same access again.

  P29 (reading along with another instance) talks to machines on the local
  network and finds them over Bonjour. Since macOS 15 both are behind the
  local network permission, which is only asked for when the app says why and
  names the service type it browses for.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Fluestr transcribes the intercom channels of your audio interface locally. Nothing is sent anywhere.</string>
    <key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Fluestr finds other Fluestr instances on your network so you can read along with what they transcribe, and lets them read along with this one.</string>
    <key>NSBonjourServices</key>
    <array>
      <string>_fluestr._tcp</string>
    </array>
  </dict>
</plist>
